Keep the v1.3.0-safe kernels on AMD/ATI adapters; leave every other vendor fast.

The 0009 guard turns vec flash-attn off through the probed subgroup width
only. A Dawn D3D12 path on GCN can probe 32 while the hardware still runs
wave64, so the guard can pass on a Radeon and leave decode on the vec
kernel, whose variable-delta subgroupShuffleDown is the pattern wave64 has
miscompiled. The correctness probe now also reads the adapter vendor and
architecture, and ggml_webgpu_adapter_is_amd() recognizes AMD/ATI: an
"amd"/"ati" vendor string, or a "gcn-*", "rdna-*", "gfx*" architecture as
Dawn reports it. AMD decodes with the tile shader, as 0009 already does for
a wide subgroup. NVIDIA, Apple, Intel, and any unknown vendor keep the
fast paths of main and pay one string compare; no probe or kernel is added
for them.

The 0012 argmax node also runs on AMD although it was measured on NVIDIA
only, and a wrong index is a wrong token. The graph gets that node only
when the output device is not this backend's AMD adapter, which the new
ggml_backend_webgpu_dev_is_amd() reports. AMD reads the logits back and
scans them on the CPU, the sampling of v1.3.0; every other output device,
CPU included, builds the graph exactly as before this patch.

The probe log carries the vendor next to the vec=on/off it already printed.
The degenerate-output detector and the per-piece CPU retry of #63 stay
unchanged, so a broken decode still falls back instead of showing garbage.

